# NWA API — environment contract (Day 1).
# Every var below is REQUIRED and Zod-validated at boot: a missing or
# malformed value fails the process fast (src/env.ts), never a half-booted
# server. Copy to `.env`, fill real values. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# Vars marked [Day N] are reserved now (contract locked once) but not
# exercised until that day; placeholders below let the scaffold boot today.

# --- Runtime ---
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
# LOG_LEVEL: fatal|error|warn|info|debug|trace. In PRODUCTION, 'fatal' is
# REFUSED at boot (src/env.ts) — pino skips the logMethod hook for calls
# suppressed below the active level, so LOG_LEVEL=fatal would silently kill
# error-level paging while the process looked healthy. Leave it at info.
LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Postgres (Day 0 lock #3: Supabase's bundled Postgres, app-owned access) ---
# Privileged app role on the Postgres connection string. No PostgREST / no
# Supabase client SDK for data / no RLS — authz is the API layer.
# Supabase direct connection (port 5432, session-mode — required for Day-2
# `SET LOCAL app.actor`). Do NOT append ?sslmode=... — TLS is driven by
# DATABASE_SSL_CA below, not the connection string.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:YOUR_DB_PASSWORD@db.YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# CA cert that signed the Postgres server cert. Supabase's direct connection
# uses Supabase's own CA (not in Node's trust store) — download it from
# dashboard → Project Settings → Database → SSL Configuration, save as
# api/certs/supabase-ca.crt. Verified TLS (rejectUnauthorized stays true);
# we teach Node the CA rather than disabling verification. Leave UNSET only
# for a bare local Postgres with no TLS.
DATABASE_SSL_CA=./certs/supabase-ca.crt

# --- Redis (server-side cache + rate limit + sessions) ---
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# --- Supabase Auth (Day 0 lock #2: JWKS verify) — wired Day 2a ---
# The project must be on ASYMMETRIC JWT signing keys (Dashboard → Auth → JWT
# Keys; RS256/ES256). Legacy HS256-shared-secret projects' JWKS won't verify.
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json
SUPABASE_JWT_AUD=authenticated
SUPABASE_JWT_ISS=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co/auth/v1

# Standard Webhooks signing secret for the Supabase "user created" auth hook
# → POST /auth/webhook [public, signed]. Wired Day 2b.
#
# Supabase side: an auth hook / webhook that fires on user creation (the
# invite/admin-create flow) and POSTs to /auth/webhook with Standard Webhooks
# headers (webhook-id / webhook-timestamp / webhook-signature). The auth
# user's metadata MUST carry the fields the mirror row's NOT-NULL columns
# need, or the webhook 422s with the exact missing list:
#   owners (default): raw_user_meta_data { name, phone,
#           location ∈ "Fayetteville, AR"|"Bentonville, AR" } + record.email
#   staff:  raw_user_meta_data { name, app_role ∈ owner-shanthi|trainer|office,
#           location? }   (app_role present ⇒ provisioned as staff)
SUPABASE_AUTH_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_placeholder

# --- Stripe (test-mode keys in dev/staging) — reserved, wired Day 14/15 ---
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_placeholder
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_placeholder

# --- Scheduler (pg_cron + pg_net signs into POST /workers/tick) — Day 16 ---
# Generate a real secret for staging/prod (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
SCHEDULER_WEBHOOK_SECRET=scheduler_placeholder

# --- Cloudflare R2 (private media) — reserved, wired Day 17 ---
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=placeholder
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=placeholder
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=placeholder
R2_BUCKET=nwa-media-dev

# --- Observability / paging (Day 20) — src/lib/observability.ts ---
# SENTRY_DSN is THE PAGER: every pino line at level >= 50 (SURPLUS REFUND,
# LOST HOLD, abandoned refunds, post-commit swallows, unhandled 500s) is
# forwarded to Sentry, which alerts a human.
#
#   - Unset (dev/test/staging default): the seam is a NO-OP. Zero network
#     traffic, zero behavior change. Alarms still print to the log.
#   - PRODUCTION: REQUIRED. `NODE_ENV=production` without it refuses to boot,
#     because a production process that pages nobody is exactly the failure
#     this seam exists to prevent (2026-08-24: 12000c refunded, nobody told).
#
# Form: https://<public_key>@<host>/<project_id> — copy it from Sentry
# (Project Settings → Client Keys). Host-injected in production (Railway env
# vars), never committed; a DSN in git is a public write key for the project.
# The project id must be digits and must NOT start with a zero. `0042` is
# digits and is not a project id; neither is `0`, which is the project id in
# SENTRY'S OWN EXAMPLE DSN and was the placeholder on this very line until
# D20-A5.4. Sentry 404s both silently, forever, on a process that reports a
# healthy pager — so both fail CLOSED at boot (D20-A4 §A4.5 N1 + D20-A5.4).
# The placeholder below is deliberately NOT copy-pasteable into production for
# that reason: paste YOUR project id, or the boot refuses.
# A path-prefixed (self-hosted) DSN is refused for the same fail-closed reason.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://examplepublickey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/424242

# One-shot proof that a DEPLOYED process reaches a human phone. Set it to true,
# redeploy, wait for the page, then unset. Fires exactly one error-level alarm
# right after the server binds — through the pino tap, so a page proves the
# WHOLE chain (pino -> hook -> captureAlarm -> transport -> Sentry -> phone),
# not just the last hop. Unset or false anywhere else.
#
# CASE-INSENSITIVE: true/TRUE/True and false/FALSE/False are all accepted
# (D20-A4 §A4.4.3). It is a diagnostic typed into a dashboard, and as a strict
# enum a capitalisation meant four crash-boots and a FAILED DEPLOY. Anything
# else (1, yes, on) is still refused, and the refusal names what is accepted.
# SENTRY_BOOT_SMOKE=false
